    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Deccan dynasty that ruled from Vatapi, modern Badami in northern Karnataka, from about 543 until 753.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#harsha">Harsha</a> on the Narmada and ruled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>.</li><li>Its temples at Badami, Aihole and Pattadakal mark the move from rock-cut caves to free-standing stone temples.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Aihole inscription of 634 names the poets <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kalidasa">Kalidasa</a> and Bharavi, giving one of the earliest firm dates by which Kalidasa’s works were already famous.</p></aside>
    </section>

